- summary: |
    Pinned pyjevsim==1.3.1 in pysdk/pyproject.toml's [project.optional-dependencies]
    pyjevsim extra. Discovered via `pip index versions pyjevsim`; available
    PyPI versions are 1.0.0, 1.3.0, 1.3.1. Upstream is github.com/cbchoi/pyjevsim
    (branches: main, develop; tags: v1.0.0).

    BLOCKING ISSUE: The orchestrator-frozen smoke test
    (pysdk/tests/spec/m4/test_spec_m4_pyjevsim_smoke.py) asserts that pyjevsim
    exports `CoupledModel` and `AtomicModel`. NO published pyjevsim version
    (1.0.0, 1.3.0, 1.3.1) and NO upstream branch (main, develop) exports
    those names. The actual API is:
        CoupledModel  ->  pyjevsim.StructuralModel
        AtomicModel   ->  pyjevsim.BehaviorModel

    Verified by:
      - `python3 -c "import pyjevsim; print(dir(pyjevsim))"` on each version
      - `gh api repos/cbchoi/pyjevsim/contents/pyjevsim/__init__.py?ref=main`
      - `gh api repos/cbchoi/pyjevsim/contents/pyjevsim/__init__.py?ref=develop`
      - `gh api search/code "CoupledModel repo:cbchoi/pyjevsim"` -> 0 hits
      - `gh api search/code "AtomicModel repo:cbchoi/pyjevsim"` -> 0 hits

    The test FAILS with the diagnostic exactly as designed by its author:
        AssertionError: pyjevsim ? is missing required symbols:
        ['CoupledModel', 'AtomicModel']. Either pin to an older version in
        pyproject.toml or update the bridge in pysdk/pyjevsim_bridge/.

    Per the W5B brief: I attempted all three remediation paths and stopped:
      1. Pin an older version with the expected names — none exists.
      2. Update _protocol.py — does not help; the spec test imports `pyjevsim`
         directly via importlib.import_module and uses hasattr() on the real
         module, not on _protocol.
      3. Modify the spec test — file is orchestrator-frozen; not done.

    Per W5B brief failure-mode guidance ("If you can't get the smoke test to
    PASS in a reasonable time (~10 min of poking), STOP and report"), I
    pinned 1.3.1 (latest stable) and surfaced the situation rather than
    silently mutating the spec test or monkey-patching pyjevsim (forbidden
    per docs/agent-c-pysdk.md §7).

    RECOMMENDED ORCHESTRATOR ACTIONS (pick one):
      (a) Authorize me (or another sub-agent) to update the smoke test's
          required-symbols list to ["StructuralModel", "BehaviorModel"]
          (and update docs/agent-c-pysdk.md §1 + §6 + §7 mapping table to
          match the real pyjevsim 1.3.x API names). Bridge code in
          pyjevsim_bridge/ already uses the Protocol-based names so no
          functional change is required.
      (b) Patch upstream pyjevsim 1.3.x to add backward-compatible aliases
          (`CoupledModel = StructuralModel`, `AtomicModel = BehaviorModel`)
          and release 1.3.2. The cbchoi/pyjevsim maintainer is the same as
          gorti's (you), so this is feasible.
      (c) Drop the smoke test's stricter assertion to a soft "imports OK"
          check and let the bridge's Protocol shims be the only contract.

